# Trivy ignore list — transitive vulnerabilities that cannot be safely fixed
# via pnpm.overrides without breaking a consumer. Each entry documents why it
# is accepted. Review periodically.

# valibot ReDoS in EMOJI_REGEX (CVE-2025-66020)
# Source: sats-connect@3.0.1 -> @sats-connect/core@0.4.1 -> valibot@0.42.1
#         (used only by @to-nexus/appkit-adapter-bitcoin)
# Why accepted: the only patched line is valibot@1.x, a breaking major that
# @sats-connect/core@0.4.1 does not support (forcing it fails the bitcoin
# adapter typecheck). The ReDoS is in an emoji-validation regex that is not on
# the wallet-connect input path, so it is not exploitable in this context.
# Remove once sats-connect ships a release built against valibot@1.x.
CVE-2025-66020

# bigint-buffer buffer overflow in toBigIntLE() (CVE-2025-3194)
# Source: @solana/web3.js dependency tree.
# Why accepted: no patched version exists (status: affected, no fix released).
# Nothing to upgrade to. Re-evaluate when bigint-buffer ships a fix.
CVE-2025-3194

# parse-duration ReDoS (CVE-2025-25283)
# Source: caver-js -> ipfs-http-client@49.0.4 -> ipfs-core-utils -> parse-duration@0.4.4
# Why accepted: the only patched line is parse-duration@2.x, which is ESM-only
# (`type: module`) and would break the CJS ipfs-http-client@49 that require()s it.
# This sits in caver-js's bundled IPFS tree, which the SDK does not exercise, and
# the ReDoS is not on any wallet/transaction input path.
CVE-2025-25283

# vite server.fs.deny bypass on Windows alternate paths (CVE-2026-53571)
# Source: vite@5.4.x (devDependency — build tool only, never deployed as a server)
# Why accepted: fixed versions are 6.4.3 / 7.3.5 / 8.0.16. vite@5.x has no patch
# release. The vulnerability requires vite dev server to be exposed to untrusted
# clients on a Windows host; this repo uses vite solely as a bundler (vite build)
# and does not run vite server in any deployed environment. Impact is zero.
# Re-evaluate when vite@5 ships a patch or when the project upgrades to vite@6+.
CVE-2026-53571

# node-forge RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature forgery (CVE-2026-85393)
# Source: node-forge@1.4.0 (transitive; pinned via pnpm.overrides to ^1.4.0)
# Why accepted: Trivy status is "affected" — no patched release exists yet, so
# there is nothing to upgrade to. The SDK does not verify RSA PKCS#1 v1.5
# signatures with node-forge. Re-evaluate when node-forge ships a fix.
CVE-2026-85393

# vite launch-editor command injection (CVE-2026-112942)
# Source: vite@5.4.x (devDependency — build tool only, never deployed as a server)
# Why accepted: fixed versions are 6.4.4 / 7.3.7 / 8.x. vite@5.x has no patch
# release (same situation as CVE-2026-53571 above). The issue is in the vite dev
# server's open-in-editor path; this repo uses vite solely as a bundler
# (vite build) and never runs the dev server in a deployed environment.
# Re-evaluate when the project upgrades to vite@6+.
CVE-2026-112942

# zod unbounded array validation DoS (CVE-2023-54404)
# Source: zod@3.22.4 / zod@3.25.76 (packages/sdk, packages/wallet, packages/experimental
#         and transitive deps). zod@4.x is already bumped to 4.6.6 via pnpm.overrides.
# Why accepted: the only patched version is 4.6.6; the zod 3.x line has no patch
# release, and moving the SDK's direct zod@3 dependency to v4 is a breaking API
# change for consumers. Re-evaluate when the SDK migrates to zod@4.
CVE-2023-54404
